;; The entries were deleted only after that run, never on the strength of the
;; compiler version -- the rule this file was written to enforce. If one comes
;; back, the checker exits 3 and names it; it does not belong here again unless
;; a decision is taken to tolerate it.
;;
;; CLASSIFY WITH THE CHECKER, NOT WITH A REBUILD. This checker answers "which
;; committed objects carry this" for the whole tree from objdump alone -- no
;; compile, no amu, seconds. Comparing a rebuild against the committed bytes
;; answers the same question indirectly, costs a compile per object, and is
;; asymmetric: bytes NOT moving is sound evidence of safety (though it assumes
;; the fix is complete for the shape, which the checker need not assume), while
;; bytes moving is not evidence of a defect at all. Measured on this very
;; sweep: 76 of 95 objects changed bytes while the shape was present in 4.
;; Reading movement as risk would have flagged 72 clean objects.
;;
;; A rebuild comparison is a good CORROBORATOR. Worked example: qwen35-attention.o
;; and qwen35-recurrent-step.o were predicted clean by QWEN-KERNELS-2 from
;; byte-identity across the fix, independently by this checker
